{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Whose daughter are you.</b> He had already asked her 'whose daughter are you' before giving her anything, and so the account of the events proves. Another interpretation: <b>and the man took a golden נזם</b> — as it sounds; he did the proper thing, to give her a fitting gift, in order to make a name for himself, to make known that he was the servant of a generous and wealthy man. But in the account of the events he said that he did not give her until he asked 'whose daughter are you' — to say that for their honor he gave her. <b>A golden נזם</b> — that the Targum here differs from in the portion of ויקהל and in the portion of מטות. נזם applies to the nose and to the ear." "<b>And two bracelets upon her hands.</b> Defective (spelling), and it is as though written 'and two bracelets he placed upon her hands.'" "<b>To lodge.</b> A noun — a lodging house, an inn where people are accustomed to stay overnight to lodge; just as one says לדין from ירב ריב, so one says לין from וילין לין."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:38.715052539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}